{{- /*
~/.config/mise/config.toml — the global mise tool set, merged from a shared base
and exactly one variant.

DIVISION OF LABOUR (unchanged, and it lives here now because the rendered file
carries no comments): mise owns the language runtimes, the registry backends
("npm:" / "cargo:" / "pipx:"), and its own internals. Standalone GitHub-release
CLI binaries are NOT mise's job — they come from .chezmoiexternals/ (grouped by
domain: ai-agents / dev-tools / vcs / k8s / system / fonts). Add a new standalone
CLI there, not here.

bun is the one runtime that is NOT here. It ships a single GitHub-release binary,
so .chezmoiexternals/dev-tools.toml delivers it with a committed version and
sha256 through the release lock. mise pins "latest" against a lockfile that is
not in this repository, so bun's version would be decided by whenever each host
last ran `mise install`. Do not add it back.

WHY A MERGE AND NOT AN INCLUDE. dot_config/git/config.tmpl and dot_ssh/config.tmpl
inline a sibling fragment as TEXT, which works because their formats tolerate a
repeated section header. TOML does not: a second [tools] table is a parse error,
so a textual split would have to be shaped around where the tables happen to
open. Merging parsed maps has no such constraint.

Two consequences, both accepted. Comments do not survive toToml, which is why the
ones worth keeping are in these sources rather than in the rendered file. And the
output is normalized — inline tables become sub-tables, arrays of inline tables
become [[array.of.tables]], keys sort. mise reads TOML, not text, so this is
semantics-preserving; .chezmoitemplates/facts.tmpl records the same sorted-output
property as the thing that makes a generated file diffable.
*/ -}}
{{- $facts := includeTemplate "facts.tmpl" . | fromYaml -}}
{{- $variant := "baremetal" -}}
{{- if $facts.container -}}{{- $variant = "container" -}}{{- end -}}
{{- $base := include (joinPath .chezmoi.sourceFile ".." ".config_base") | fromToml -}}
{{- $overlay := include (joinPath .chezmoi.sourceFile ".." (printf ".config_%s" $variant)) | fromToml -}}
{{ mergeOverwrite $base $overlay | toToml }}
